---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Cameron Oliver | Fractional COO & Growth Consultant"
  description="Cameron Oliver is a fractional COO and business operations consultant who helps founders build systems that make growth predictable without burning out."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <!-- HERO / INTRO -->
  <section class="border-b border-hairline px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-[1200px] flex-col items-center gap-12 md:flex-row md:gap-16">
      <div class="flex-1">
        <p class="mb-5 font-mono text-[11.5px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-moss">
          The Operator
        </p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl leading-[1.1] text-ink sm:text-5xl md:text-[48px]">
          I'm an operator, <em>not a theorist.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-[54ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-fern">
          I've spent a decade inside fast-growing startups, from employee #3 to 100+, usually as the person leaders call when things start breaking.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex-shrink-0">
        <img
          src="/images/about-photo.jpeg"
          alt="Cameron Oliver"
          class="w-72 rounded-[14px] border border-hairline md:w-96"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- STORY -->
  <section class="border-b border-hairline bg-parchment-deep px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[800px]">
      <p class="doc-label text-ink"><b>1.0</b>The Pattern</p>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink">
        <p>
          My work has always sat at the intersection of operations, go-to-market, delivery, and product. Translating vision into the systems, roles, and rhythms that make a company work.
        </p>
        <p>
          After enough years in the trenches, the same pattern became impossible to ignore:
        </p>

        <div>
          {[
            'Founders making every decision themselves because nobody else had the context.',
            'Teams working hard but not on the same thing.',
            'Revenue unpredictable because nobody understood how the business actually created value.',
            'Bad hires, unclear priorities, and founders carrying the anxiety of the entire company on their shoulders.',
          ].map((item) => (
            <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3.5 border-b border-dashed border-hairline py-3 text-[16px] font-medium text-ink">
              <span class="cbx">X</span>
              {item}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <p>
          Every one of those companies thought it had a revenue problem. Every one of them actually had an operating problem wearing a revenue costume.
        </p>

        <p>
          Growth Map is my way of giving founders what I always wished every company I operated had:
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-4 pl-1">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-moss"></span>
            A clear picture of how the business actually makes money
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-moss"></span>
            Clarity on what drives outcomes vs. what just keeps people busy
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-moss"></span>
            A practical way to make decisions week to week without guessing
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-moss"></span>
            A path to grow without chaos or burnout
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY ME -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[800px]">
      <p class="doc-label text-ink"><b>2.0</b>Objections, Handled</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-7 text-3xl leading-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">
        Why work with me instead of&hellip;
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-9 space-y-6">
        <div class="rounded-[14px] border border-hairline bg-white/50 p-7">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-ink">"&hellip;hiring a full-time COO?"</h3>
          <p class="mt-2.5 leading-relaxed text-fern">
            A good full-time COO costs $200K–$400K+ and takes months to ramp up. Most owner-led companies between $1M and $50M don't need a full-time executive. They need someone who's done this before, can build the system fast, and transfer ownership to their existing team.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-[14px] border border-hairline bg-white/50 p-7">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-ink">"&hellip;reading a business book or taking a course?"</h3>
          <p class="mt-2.5 leading-relaxed text-fern">
            Books give you frameworks. I give you implementation. The gap between knowing what to do and actually doing it inside a messy, real business is where I live. I've built operating systems inside fast-growing companies, not in a classroom.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-[14px] border border-hairline bg-white/50 p-7">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-ink">"&hellip;using a big consulting firm?"</h3>
          <p class="mt-2.5 leading-relaxed text-fern">
            Big firms send you junior analysts who produce slide decks. I do the work myself, in the trenches with your team. You get a senior operator, not a presentation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
